      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;div id="resg-s1-148571" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 8640;         --source-height: 5760;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8640x5760+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Fc2%2F7c93157648a897c328e54e703d4c%2Fap26289837988678.jpg" class="img" alt="A roof engulfed in flames is seen during the Norte Fire on Friday, Oct. 16, 2026, in San Juan Capistrano, Calif." fetchpriority="high" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A roof engulfed in flames is seen during the Norte Fire on Friday, Oct. 16, 2026, in San Juan Capistrano, Calif.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Jae C. Hong/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;A fast-moving fire fueled by high winds burned at least six homes in Southern California on Friday, engulfing expensive coastal properties and prompting thousands to evacuate.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Black smoke — visible from miles away — billowed over tennis courts and swimming pools while firefighters doused blazing homes in San Juan Capistrano in Orange County. Some homeowners sprayed water on their properties before heeding evacuation orders.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Two firefighters were taken to the hospital with heat-related injuries, officials said. Authorities have not said how the blaze, which was less than a square mile as of Friday evening, started.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Had these winds been a little bit stronger, a little bit different direction, this could have been a whole lot worse," said San Clemente Mayor Rick Loeffler.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Howard Hart, a councilmember for San Juan Capistrano, said he and his wife doused their roof with water and moved propane tanks away from their home before they evacuated Friday with a to-go bag.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Laura Hart hasn't had to evacuate due to fire in the more than five decades she's lived in the community, she said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"This doesn't usually happen to us, we usually see it on the news," she said. "We always pray to God it's not us, but yeah, it was today."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The Norte fire started in the coastal city of San Clemente, and wind drove it into San Juan Capistrano. An evacuation shelter has opened in each city. By Friday night, about 16,000 residents had been ordered to evacuate, said Fire Chief TJ McGovern, of the Orange County Fire Authority.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;It was one of several fires in the region hit by dry, warm gusts known as Santa Anas, which blow from the interior and toward the coast. The strongest winds were expected through Friday afternoon, but conditions that increase the fire risk were expected to last through Saturday night, with a heat advisory in effect until 8 p.m. Saturday on the Orange County and San Diego County coast, the National Weather Service said.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Tens of thousands of people in the state are without power after their electricity was turned off. A separate fire by the Marine Corps base Camp Pendleton shut down for hours a section of Interstate 5 that is a major artery connecting Orange County to San Diego. That added hours to commutes throughout Southern California.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The coastal cities are surrounded by hillsides. San Juan Capistrano, a city of 35,000, is known for horse trails and the historic Mission San Juan Capistrano. San Clemente, which is home to 62,000 people, is known as a "Spanish village by the sea" and popular with beachgoers and surfers.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"The fire is right up on the city," said Victor Cabral, a San Clemente Council member. "It's on the perimeter of our homes on the north end."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Nine schools were also closed Friday in San Juan Capistrano, the Capistrano Unified School District said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Nearby residents were also on edge as smoke darkened the sky.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Wyoming resident Shannon Needham was visiting her mother at her assisted living facility in Dana Point just north of San Clemente when she learned about the fire.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The facility director told her that two buses would be on standby in case they needed to evacuate, Needham said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"You could hear the fire trucks, you could hear the helicopters and everything above. And it was so smoky, it was just dark smoke," Needham said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Some of California's worst wildfires have been sparked by power equipment, and utilities in recent years have begun proactively shutting off power in dry winds. More than 118,000 customers in California were without electricity as of Friday, according to poweroutage.com.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The weather service also issued a red flag warning for parts of central and Northern California through Friday morning, saying any fires would spread rapidly.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
