ormat/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2Fbc%2Fbfd2cec64a52a1f8ce3479d71179%2Fsam.jpg" class="img" alt="A work by Thomas in Flagstaff, Arizona." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 2014 installation on a water tank near Cow Springs, Az.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          &lt;a   href="https://jetsonorama.net/" class="Link"  target="_blank"   &gt;jetsonorama&lt;/a&gt;                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ephemeral Artwork For Navajo People&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;On a morning last Spring, Thomas and I drove north out of Flagstaff in his hatchback to check out some of the work.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Clusters of ponderosa pine forests gave way to open desert. Ahead of us, the ribbon of highway disappeared into a sea of sagebrush and yellow grasses. Then we reached a cluster of derelict buildings, some of them covered with spraypainted artwork.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Thomas veered off the road, coasting to a stop in front of an abandoned cinderblock structure.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Lean, bearded, dreadlocks tucked inside a canvas cap, Thomas approached the tiny structure, which might have been a storage shed at one time, but the roof and door were gone now.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"This is the natural evolution of a piece in the desert. It's breaking down," he said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5779751-101" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5779751-101" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;We stepped inside.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"This is part of a sight and sound installation," Thomas said, scanning the walls. "Looks like the sound may have stopped."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;A 10-foot wide, black and white image covered the back wall, part of an art piece spotlighting the devastating health effects of uranium mining among Navajo workers during the cold war.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"My image is of Kee John," Thomas said. "Who died at a young age from cancer related to his work in a uranium mine."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;In the photo, a young Navajo man wears a hardhat with a headlamp, and operates uranium mining equipment. But the image was fading, pieces of the installation were peeling off the walls.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The wind howled, sunlight blared in from overhead, through the wooden, skeletal remains of the ceiling.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Then suddenly a solar powered speaker kicked on, and we heard the tinny, garbled sounds of a Geiger counter. This was what was left of the installation's audio. Thomas chuckled.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Yeah this is on its last leg," he said, nodding to a speaker tucked in between the ceiling joists. "But it's impressive. It's been running three and half years now, non-stop."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148249" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4000;         --source-height: 2667;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F73%2Fff%2F13f5f4304b07a36d0142c5596029%2Fimg-9799.jpg" class="img" alt="Chip Thomas stands in the middle of an abandoned cinder block in Flagstaff, Az. The structure holds one of his sight and sound installations." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Chip Thomas stands in the middle of an abandoned cinder block building north of Flagstaff, Az. The structure holds a sight and sound installation, spotlighting the devastating health effects of uranium mining among Navajo workers during the cold war.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Adam Burke/KSUT                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;All of Thomas' work is conceptual in this way: the physical materials are no match for the unrelenting wind and sand.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"The work is ephemeral," Thomas said. "It's paper against the elements, and the elements … Mother Nature always wins."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Down the highway 25 minutes, we stopped at a roadside stand where vendors were selling table-loads of turquoise and silver jewelry.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Torrey Charley was working at one of the stands. She's 29, and first started seeing Thomas' artwork as a teenager.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"I was like, 'oh wow, you know, there's somebody that's interested in the community,'" she said. "You know, livestock and kids or the elders within the community."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Charley is Navajo, or Diné, as Navajo people call themselves.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"I think as a teenager, I was like, 'dang I wonder who this is?' you know? And I probably assumed that it was a young Diné artist, doing photography," Charley said, laughing. "Finding out he was a doctor, that was interesting."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;From Outlaw Artist To Community Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Born and raised in North Carolina, Chip Thomas moved to the Navajo Nation in 1987 to work as a family physician in a remote, underserved region.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"I had thought that because of the isolation I would be there initially for two years," Thomas said. "But my two years turned into 36."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;He spent time with patients outside of the clinic, helping haul water, stack firewood, and shear sheep. As he grew closer to Navajo people, Thomas started photographing them.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;"There was, you know, a degree of trust," Thomas said. "I could stick a camera, not literally in someone's face, but I could get closer physically than a stranger could, and tell more intimate stories.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Thomas did not consider himself an artist until 2009. That was the year a friend showed him the work of the &lt;a href="https://www.jr-art.net/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;French street artist JR&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, who covered the walls of urban buildings with giant images. Thomas was 52 at the time.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"It was like oh my god this is it," Thomas recalled. "This person has figured out how to take a documentary black and white photograph, blow it up to scale and use it as street art. My mind was blown!"&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148257" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 6000;         --source-height: 4002;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x4002+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F85%2Fd1%2F51d56dca4f03ad005fc983b1665e%2Fthomas-2026-hi-res-download-1.jpg" class="img" alt="Chip Thomas." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 The MacArthur Foundation named Thomas as one its 2026 Fellows for, "transforming overlooked and neglected spaces into powerful public works grounded in community experience and histories."                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          &lt;i&gt;John D. and Catherine T. MacArthur Foundation&lt;/i&gt;                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;This was the era of Banksy, Shepherd Fairey and countless masked, anonymous street artists who put up work in public spaces without permission. Documentaries like&lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exit_Through_the_Gift_Shop" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt; Exit Through the Giftshop&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, celebrated the social impact of outlaw artists.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;At first, Thomas worked in secret too. He adopted the street artist name Jetsonorama, a moniker drawn from his given name James Edward Thomas, Jr., i.e. "son of JET".&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Sneaking around, getting artwork up, usually at night, is a rush," Thomas said. "I was living the life of my street art heroes."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Then one time, he returned to photograph a piece he'd pasted on a dilapidated roadside stand near Bitter Springs, Arizona. It was an image of a Code Talker, one of the Navajo Marines who used their native language to transmit messages among US allies during World War II.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;When Thomas returned to the installation, he found several men working on the building.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"I said, 'hey do you mind if I take a picture of this wall?'" Thomas recalled. "And they said, 'yeah, you may as well, everybody else has been.'"&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;So many tourists were stopping to take photos, that the owners had decided to repair the stand to start using it again.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;It was the first time Thomas revealed himself as an artist&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"So I said to them, 'yeah I put that picture up,'" Thomas said. "And they were excited. They thanked me and said, 'before you go would you be interested in putting something on the other side, to stop traffic coming from the other direction?'"&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Thomas still works in secret sometimes, putting up work at night, without permission. But over time, he's decided that community trust and dialogue adds a depth and meaning to his work.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"On the spectrum between outlaw and community engaged artist, I am definitely on the community engagement end of things at this point," Thomas said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148433" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 1600;         --source-height: 539;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F31%2Fb2%2F9e7c8ac24fd18c2d2d590d3055be%2Fchip-thomas-bw-2.jpg" class="img" alt="Thomas&amp;#039; large-scale installations depict ordinary life on the Navajo Nation, with work that often interacts with the vast arid landscapes. Though he uses abandoned buildings, Thomas also places work on roadside stands where Navajo vendors sell jewelry and food." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Thomas' large-scale installations depict ordinary life on the Navajo Nation, with work that often interacts with the vast arid landscapes. Though he uses abandoned buildings, Thomas also places work on roadside stands where Navajo vendors sell jewelry and food.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          &lt;a   href="https://jetsonorama.net/" class="Link"  target="_blank"   &gt;jetsonorama&lt;/a&gt;                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Landscape of Disorienting Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;As a public artist, Thomas works in a landscape of disorienting scale and inscrutable distances. The Navajo Nation is a 27,000 square mile territory that covers portions of Arizona, New Mexico and southern Utah.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;For outsiders, this is a geography containing points of interest, like Monument Valley, Lake Powell, and the Grand Canyon.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Thomas is concerned with the spaces in between and the community life that's often invisible to tourists passing through.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"People tend to look at a landscape like that as just kind of bleak and empty and worthless," said art historian Keven Moore, who curated &lt;a href="https://www.fotofocus.org/fotofocus-exhibition/chip-thomas-and-the-painted-desert-project/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;a retrospective of Thomas' work at FotoFocus in Cincinnati&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; a few years ago.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"To drive across the desert and see a photograph, black and white photograph, pasted to a building of a smiling girl or an old couple. It's striking, it's surreal, it's actually haunting," Moore said, noting that Thomas' artwork is not for sale and free to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"It feels mysterious," Moore added. "It's sort of like: who did this? Why did they do this? You see something like this and you … expect it to try to go to work on you, in a way. But as you sit with it, and contemplate it, you realize you don't understand what it's trying to do to you. And then you understand that maybe it's just trying to exist. Maybe it's trying to get you to exist with it. Maybe that's a good place to be, with art."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148260" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4000;         --source-height: 2667;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fdf%2F21%2F42d1803c45cb9230ca1b1bd6a953%2Fsheep-midday-close1.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fdf%2F21%2F42d1803c45cb9230ca1b1bd6a953%2Fsheep-midday-close1.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fdf%2F21%2F42d1803c45cb9230ca1b1bd6a953%2Fsheep-midday-close1.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fdf%2F21%2F42d1803c45cb9230ca1b1bd6a953%2Fsheep-midday-close1.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/di